{0 LSP Features}

{ul
  {- all docs with prefix "feature-" is considered an active feature.}
  {- an active feature should be tested against its spec. }
  {- deprecated or superseded features are named differently}
  {- a spec listed under {!specified} is written but not implemented: it is a
     feature-level spec awaiting code, not a feature the server has.}
}

{1 Principles}

{ul
  {- {b Syntax is recognized by the parser, never re-implemented here}: a
     feature that needs headings, anchors, divs or fences reads them off the
     AST ({!Lsp_lib.Anchors}, {!Lsp_lib.Link_collect}), because a second
     reading of the text is free to drift from the one that decides what the
     note actually is. The exception is completion, which by definition runs
     on text that is not yet syntax.}
}

